Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: answer D32 depth support from the device, not a table

Patch 0027 requests depth32float-stencil8 when the adapter offers it. That is
only half of the negotiation, and without this half the stack works on hardware
that happens to have the feature and fails everywhere else.

Godot does not require D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT. It prefers it and falls back to
D24_UNORM_S8_UINT -- but only when texture_is_format_supported_for_usage() says
the preferred format is unavailable. That question reaches this driver through
texture_get_usages_supported_by_format(), which answered from the static format
table: if a WGPUTextureFormat enum existed, the format was reported supported.

So on an adapter without the optional feature:

  adapter lacks depth32float-stencil8
      -> the shell correctly omits it from requiredFeatures
      -> this driver still reports D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT supported
      -> Godot selects D32 and never reaches its own D24 fallback
      -> texture creation fails, with no fallback left

The authority is the created GPUDevice's enabled feature set, not the adapter's
capabilities and not the header enum. This mirrors the gating the same function
already applies to the BC/ETC2/ASTC compression families.

Reported once at device creation under --verbose, so a bug report from an
unfamiliar adapter says which depth format was chosen and why.

NOT VERIFIED ON HARDWARE LACKING THE FEATURE. The verification host (Tesla P40)
exposes depth32float-stencil8, so the fallback branch has never executed here.
It is recorded as unmeasured in docs/architecture/webgpu-runtime-status.md
rather than claimed.

diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
--- a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.cpp
@@ -926,6 +926,10 @@
 	// Optional texture-compression families. The JS shell opts in to these when
 	// the adapter supports them; we must match that here so Godot only advertises
 	// the corresponding DataFormats when they'll actually work.
+	// Optional; see texture_get_usages_supported_by_format for why the DEVICE and
+	// not the adapter is the authority here.
+	has_depth32float_stencil8 = wgpuDeviceHasFeature(device, WGPUFeatureName_Depth32FloatStencil8);
+	print_verbose(vformat("WebGPU: depth32float-stencil8 %s", has_depth32float_stencil8 ? "enabled" : "unavailable (Godot will use D24_UNORM_S8_UINT)"));
 	has_texture_compression_bc = wgpuDeviceHasFeature(device, WGPUFeatureName_TextureCompressionBC);
 	has_texture_compression_etc2 = wgpuDeviceHasFeature(device, WGPUFeatureName_TextureCompressionETC2);
 	has_texture_compression_astc = wgpuDeviceHasFeature(device, WGPUFeatureName_TextureCompressionASTC);
@@ -2240,6 +2244,16 @@
 		case DATA_FORMAT_D16_UNORM_S8_UINT:
 		case DATA_FORMAT_D24_UNORM_S8_UINT:
 		case DATA_FORMAT_D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT:
+			// depth32float-stencil8 is an OPTIONAL WebGPU device feature. Godot
+			// prefers D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT and falls back to D24_UNORM_S8_UINT, but
+			// only if this call says the preferred one is unsupported. Answering
+			// from the static format table instead of the device would make Godot
+			// choose D32 on an adapter that cannot create it, and texture creation
+			// would fail later with no fallback left -- a bug that is invisible on
+			// hardware that happens to have the feature.
+			if (!has_depth32float_stencil8) {
+				return 0;
+			}
 			is_depth_stencil = true;
 			break;
 
@@ -9286,11 +9300,11 @@
 		case SUPPORTS_FRAGMENT_SHADER_WITH_ONLY_SIDE_EFFECTS:
 			// WebGPU requires a render pass to have at least one color attachment or
 			// a depth-stencil attachment; a pass with neither is a validation error
-			// ("No attachment was specified."). Reporting true made the cluster builder
+			// ("No attachment was specified"). Reporting true made the cluster builder
 			// take framebuffer_format_create_empty() and fail every frame. Reporting
-			// false selects Godot's existing USE_ATTACHMENT path, which binds a
-			// throwaway color target -- the cost of one unused attachment, in exchange
-			// for the pass actually executing.
+			// false selects the USE_ATTACHMENT variant, which binds a throwaway color
+			// target -- the cost of one unused attachment, in exchange for the pass
+			// actually executing.
 			return false;
 		case SUPPORTS_IMAGE_ATOMIC_32_BIT:
 			return false; // WebGPU has no image atomics support.
diff --git a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.h b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.h
--- a/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.h
+++ b/drivers/webgpu/rendering_device_driver_webgpu.h
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@
 	// shell at device creation; the driver must only report the corresponding
 	// DataFormats as supported when the feature is actually enabled, otherwise
 	// texture creation will fail at runtime.
+	bool has_depth32float_stencil8 = false;
 	bool has_texture_compression_bc = false;
 	bool has_texture_compression_etc2 = false;
 	bool has_texture_compression_astc = false;
